The toolchain audit (session spec-isa-audit, 2026-10-28): the vendor
toolchain's own decoder table (in its objdump), assembler and compiler
know instruction forms fwtest could not run, or ran wrongly. This patch
takes the ones the compiler emits with the firmware's flags
(-mcpu=r3 -mfprev1) and the rest of the float forms:

- The FPU's unary row (`3f e5 Xf DS`, `3f f5` a pair's head): ftoi and
  ftou rounding to even, up and down (0f 2f 3f, 4f 6f 7f), saturating as
  the truncating ones do; `R = ftof(R)` rounded to an integral value
  (cf even, df trunc, ef ceil, ff floor), which the compiler emits for
  rintf, truncf, ceilf and floorf, so C's results; `R.l = ftof(R)` (af)
  and `R = ftof(R.l)` (bf), the `__fp16` conversions, rounding to
  nearest even, the high half left as it was (the compiler's code stores
  the low half only).
- `fcmp rA, rB` (`3f e5 A4 0B`) and the flag branches `ifeq` .. `ifle`
  (`40|c0 e8|e9|ec|ed|ee`, off 2*sext16(bits 16-31)). Their byte 1 is
  the compare branches' family and bit 7 the opposite condition, so after
  an fcmp each is that family's float compare (as `iff (rA cond rB)`).
  After a testset, ifeq / ifne read its flag as before; the other
  conditions end the run as an unsupported instruction. The table had
  `ifeq` backwards only (the compiler's spin loop) and took `41 e8`, no
  instruction, for `ifne` (`c0 e8`).
- The memory row `[R+#i] op= R`: `&= ~R` (`64 e8`, op 3; the compiler's
  `*p &= ~m`) and the shifts by a register `6e e8` (op 0 `<<=`, 2 `>>=`,
  3 `>>>=`; `*p <<= n`), in the `64 e8` layout, the amount as the
  register shifts take it (bits 0-4). `6c e8` with a shift field of 0
  shifts by 32 (it shifted by 0).
- `rH_rL = d[rB+rI<<3]` / `d[rB+rI<<3] = rH_rL`: bit 19 of the plain
  indexed form scales the index by 8 (the compiler's 64-bit `p[1000]`);
  it was added unscaled.
- `rD = zcmp(rS)` (`80 e1 02 DS`; `__builtin_pi32v2_zcmp`): the sign,
  -1, 0 or 1, as the compiler folds the builtin's constants.

Fields from the vendor assembler; behaviour from the compiler's use and
constant folding, and where the toolchain leaves a detail open (NaN
results, out-of-range conversions, the conditions' sources, amounts of
32 or more) the choice above, HARDWARE-SPEC Q-28 to Q-30. The crate tests
float_rounding_to_integral, float_to_integer_rounding,
half_precision_conversions, memory_shifts_and_and_not, flag_branches,
pair_load_with_a_scaled_index and zcmp_is_the_sign, and the harness
tests forms_the_compiler_emits (tests/images/isac.c, built with the
firmware's flags) and forms_only_the_assembler_emits (isaasm.S), fail
without it. From the vendor toolchain (PROVENANCE P-1) only.

